  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN229.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṉ piriviṉkaṇ vēṟupaṭṭa talaimakaḷai vaṟpuṟuttun tōḻikkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What [SHE] said to the confidante who consoled HER who had undergone changes during the separation from HIM.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN229.1">
        <l><anchor n="1"/>pakalcey palkatirp parutiyañ celva</l>
        <l>ṉakalvāy vāṉat tāḻi pōḻnteṉa</l>
        <l><supplied>nīra</supplied>ṟa vaṟanta nirampā nīḷiṭaik</l>
        <l>kayantalaik kuḻavik kaviyukir maṭappiṭi</l>
        <l>kuḷakumaṟut tuyaṅkiya maruṅkul palavuṭaṉ</l>
        <l>pāḻūrk kurampaiyiṟ ṟōṉṟu māṅka</l>
        <l>ṇeṭuñcē ṇiṭaiya kuṉṟam pōkiya</l>
        <l>poyva lāḷar muyaṉṟucey perumporu</l>
        <l><supplied>ṇa</supplied>mmiṉ ṟāyiṉu muṭika valleṉap</l>
        <l>peruntuṉi mēva ṉalkūr kuṟumaka</l>
        <l>ṇōymalin tukutta nocivār ciṉṉīrp</l>
        <l>pallitaḻ maḻaikkaṭ pāvai māyppap</l>
        <l>poṉṉēr pacalai yūrtarap poṟivari </l>
        <l>naṉmā mēṉi tolaita ṉōkki </l>
        <l>yiṉaiya leṉṟi tōḻi ciṉaiya</l>
        <l>pācarum pīṉṟa cemmuka murukkiṉ</l>
        <l>pōtavi ḻalari koḻutit tātarun</l>
        <l>tantaḷir marāat talaṅkaṉ mīmicaic</l>
        <l>ceṅka ṇiruṅkuyi ṉayavarak kūu</l>
        <l>miṉṉiḷa vēṉilum vārā</l>
        <l>riṉṉē varutu meṉatteḷin tōrē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="9b">“Although,</l>
        <l corresp="3">on the never-ending long way that dried up when the water ceased</l>
        <l corresp="1f.">because the wheel of the spherical goer with many day-making </l>
        <l corresp="1f">rays crossed the sky of vast area,</l>
        <l>in that place, where the youthful elephant cows with enveloped toenails, many together,</l>
        <l>waists narrow as they refused the [remaining] greenery for [the sake of their] soft-headed calves,</l>
        <l corresp="4-6">appear like the huts of a village in ruin,</l>
        <l corresp="8">the great wealth to be made with effort by the deceitful man</l>
        <l corresp="7">who went to the hills that are in the far distance,</l>
        <l corresp="9">is [made] without us, let it be accomplished fast,</l>
        <l>[my] poor little girl who is attached to [her] great disgust.</l>
        <l corresp="12">While the pupils of your ample-lashed rain eyes hide</l>
        <l corresp="11">the painfully overflowing few tears that they shed as the pain increases,</l>
        <l>don’t look at the loss of the spots [and] lines  on [your] good</l>
        <l corresp="13f.">dark body while gold-like pallor creeps up,</l>
        <l corresp="15a-c">[and] despair,” you may say, friend,</l>
        <l corresp="20">– [about]  him who did not come even in sweet spring,</l>
        <l corresp="17">when, having pecked at the flowers that open [their] buds [and] eating the pollen</l>
        <l corresp="15d-16">of the red-faced Palas trees that brought forth green buds on [their] branches,</l>
        <l corresp="18">high on the swaying height of the Kadamba trees with pretty sprouts</l>
        <l corresp="19">the red-eyed dark koel calls out in longing,</l>
        <l corresp="21">he who was clear in saying “we will come now.”</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

